WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.595
Learning is not the same thing as exposure.

00:00:02.595 --> 00:00:04.650
A person can sit through a lesson, read a procedure,

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.000
or watch a demonstration and still be unable to use the idea later.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.330
In practical terms, learning means a durable change in understanding, skill, judgment,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.105
or behavior.

00:00:13.105 --> 00:00:16.690
Something has changed in what the learner can explain, decide, notice, perform,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.435
or improve.

00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:21.410
That difference matters because many training programs accidentally measure attendance,

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.560
completion, or familiarity when the real goal is usable capability.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.860
There are levels of progress.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.125
Exposure means the learner has encountered the idea.

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.620
Familiarity means the idea feels recognizable.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.730
Recall means the learner can bring information back from memory.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.180
Usable capability means the learner can apply the idea in a real situation,

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.475
with the normal messiness of time pressure, incomplete information,

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:41.820
and competing priorities.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.895
A course that only tells people what to know may create familiarity,

00:00:44.895 --> 00:00:47.530
but it rarely creates confident performance by itself.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.060
Effective learning is active.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.115
People pay attention, connect new information to what they already know, form meaning,

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:56.915
practice, receive feedback, adjust, and try again in a slightly different context.

00:00:56.915 --> 00:00:59.790
Good learning design starts with the work people need to do,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.660
not just the information they need to hear.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.400
When the desired performance is clear,

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.040
the lesson can focus attention on the important relationships,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.280
give learners enough practice to build confidence,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.620
and help them transfer the skill beyond the course.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.260
A useful test is to ask what evidence would prove the learner can do the thing.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.070
If the outcome is only, they heard the message, the design will usually stop too early.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:22.635
If the outcome is, they can recognize a situation, choose an approach, explain a tradeoff,

00:01:22.635 --> 00:01:23.680
or complete a task,

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.280
the course needs examples and practice that let those behaviors appear.
